{
  "course": "初中60短文",
  "passage": 46,
  "title": "Passage 46",
  "voice": "温暖自然英式女老师｜IndexTTS2.5 慢速教学",
  "sentences": [
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 1,
      "sourceSentenceId": 1,
      "chunkId": "s46-p01",
      "image": "assets/images/01.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p01.mp3",
      "en": "Laughter is a universal language for humans.",
      "cn": "笑是人类共同的语言。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 2,
      "sourceSentenceId": 2,
      "chunkId": "s46-p02",
      "image": "assets/images/02.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p02.mp3",
      "en": "It can help people to get on well with others.",
      "cn": "它可以帮助人们与他人和睦相处。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 3,
      "sourceSentenceId": 3,
      "chunkId": "s46-p03",
      "image": "assets/images/03.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p03.mp3",
      "en": "As children, we laugh when our parents make faces.",
      "cn": "小时候，当父母做鬼脸时，我们会笑。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 4,
      "sourceSentenceId": 4,
      "chunkId": "s46-p04",
      "image": "assets/images/04.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p04.mp3",
      "en": "Then we start to make others laugh like this.",
      "cn": "然后，我们也开始这样逗别人笑。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 5,
      "sourceSentenceId": 5,
      "chunkId": "s46-p05",
      "image": "assets/images/05.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p05.mp3",
      "en": "That's how we learn to play jokes.",
      "cn": "我们就是这样学会开玩笑的。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 6,
      "sourceSentenceId": 6,
      "chunkId": "s46-p06",
      "image": "assets/images/06.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p06.mp3",
      "en": "But is playing jokes only humans' ability?",
      "cn": "不过，开玩笑是只有人类才具有的能力吗？"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 7,
      "sourceSentenceId": 7,
      "chunkId": "s46-p07",
      "image": "assets/images/07.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p07.mp3",
      "en": "Scientists believe that some animals also have the ability.",
      "cn": "科学家认为，有些动物也具备这种能力。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 8,
      "sourceSentenceId": 8,
      "chunkId": "s46-p08",
      "image": "assets/images/08.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p08.mp3",
      "en": "Dogs are smart animals with a good nose.",
      "cn": "狗是聪明的动物，拥有灵敏的鼻子。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 9,
      "sourceSentenceId": 9,
      "chunkId": "s46-p09",
      "image": "assets/images/09.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p09.mp3",
      "en": "They often help people.",
      "cn": "它们经常帮助人类。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 10,
      "sourceSentenceId": 10,
      "chunkId": "s46-p10",
      "image": "assets/images/10.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p10.mp3",
      "en": "But sometimes we see dogs play jokes on people.",
      "cn": "但有时我们也会看到狗跟人开玩笑。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 11,
      "sourceSentenceId": 11,
      "chunkId": "s46-p11",
      "image": "assets/images/11.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p11.mp3",
      "en": "They come near slowly and then quickly run away.",
      "cn": "它们会慢慢靠近，然后迅速跑开。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 12,
      "sourceSentenceId": 12,
      "chunkId": "s46-p12",
      "image": "assets/images/12.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p12.mp3",
      "en": "This act seems silly.",
      "cn": "这种行为看似很傻。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 13,
      "sourceSentenceId": 13,
      "chunkId": "s46-p13",
      "image": "assets/images/13.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p13.mp3",
      "en": "But they may just want to have fun.",
      "cn": "但它们可能只是想找点乐子。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 14,
      "sourceSentenceId": 14,
      "chunkId": "s46-p14",
      "image": "assets/images/14.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p14.mp3",
      "en": "When dogs are guarding, they sometimes hide behind a door to scare visitors in a playful way.",
      "cn": "狗在看门时，有时会藏在门后，以一种闹着玩的方式吓唬来访者。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 15,
      "sourceSentenceId": 15,
      "chunkId": "s46-p15",
      "image": "assets/images/15.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p15.mp3",
      "en": "They fool their owners too.",
      "cn": "它们也会捉弄自己的主人。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 16,
      "sourceSentenceId": 16,
      "chunkId": "s46-p16",
      "image": "assets/images/16.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p16.mp3",
      "en": "But after a joke, they lick their owner, which is like giving a kiss to show they are friendly.",
      "cn": "但玩笑过后，它们会舔舔主人，那就像亲吻一样，表明它们是友好的。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 17,
      "sourceSentenceId": 17,
      "chunkId": "s46-p17",
      "image": "assets/images/17.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p17.mp3",
      "en": "Scientists say they have watched young apes play jokes.",
      "cn": "科学家们称，他们曾观察到小猿猴开玩笑。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 18,
      "sourceSentenceId": 18,
      "chunkId": "s46-p18",
      "image": "assets/images/18.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p18.mp3",
      "en": "The young apes quietly follow adult apes and touch them secretly to surprise them.",
      "cn": "小猿猴悄悄地跟在成年猿猴后面，偷偷地触碰它们，让它们大吃一惊。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 19,
      "sourceSentenceId": 19,
      "chunkId": "s46-p19",
      "image": "assets/images/19.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p19.mp3",
      "en": "Then they playfully wait and watch what the adults would do.",
      "cn": "然后，它们会调皮地等着看成年猿猴会做出什么反应。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 20,
      "sourceSentenceId": 20,
      "chunkId": "s46-p20",
      "image": "assets/images/20.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p20.mp3",
      "en": "This action is similar to what human children do.",
      "cn": "这种行为与人类儿童的行为相似。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 21,
      "sourceSentenceId": 21,
      "chunkId": "s46-p21",
      "image": "assets/images/21.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p21.mp3",
      "en": "Next time, when you find your pets doing something strange around you, maybe they are having jokes with you.",
      "cn": "下次，当你发现你的宠物在你身边做一些奇怪的事情时，也许它们是在和你开玩笑。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 22,
      "sourceSentenceId": 22,
      "chunkId": "s46-p22",
      "image": "assets/images/22.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p22.mp3",
      "en": "So don't be mad if your dog borrows your shoe or your cat hides your sock.",
      "cn": "所以，如果你的狗“借走”了你的鞋子，或者你的猫藏起了你的袜子，请不要生气。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 23,
      "sourceSentenceId": 23,
      "chunkId": "s46-p23",
      "image": "assets/images/23.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p23.mp3",
      "en": "They might just be trying to make you laugh.",
      "cn": "它们可能只是试图在逗你笑。"
    }
  ],
